+# aims Guide State
+
+Loop status only. Not the design record (see `src/requests/sessions.py.md`, `src/requests/adapters.py.md`).
+
+## Mode
+
+auto
+
+## Loop cursor
+
+ready-to-choose-next (adapter-owned-default-timeout: met)
+
+## Current objective
+
+**Kind:** add-feature
+
+**Objective:** The transport adapter becomes the one owner of "which timeout applies to this send": a
+configured default when the caller supplied none, the caller's value otherwise, resolved through the single
+existing timeout-resolution path. `Session` stays untouched in its timeout handling (recorded decision,
+reaffirmed by the product owner 2026-09-23).
+
+**Why now:** Product change: set a default timeout once for a session; every request through that session uses
+it unless the call passes its own. Product owner: timeouts are adapter (connection) concerns, not Session state.
+
+**Hard decision:** `Session.request` forwards `timeout=None` whether or not the caller passed it, so the adapter
+cannot tell "omitted" from "explicit None". Resolved: None means "use the default"; a call that truly wants no
+timeout passes `(None, None)` (or a urllib3 `Timeout(None, None)`). Derived from the PO constraint (no Session
+timeout logic) plus the stated safety goal (a forgotten / passed-through None must not hang).
+
+**Exit criteria:**
+- [x] Adapter with default D mounted on a session: `s.get(url)` sends with D (float → connect=read=D; tuple → separate; urllib3 Timeout → as given).
+- [x] Per-call T overrides D, for float, tuple and urllib3 Timeout.
+- [x] Explicit `timeout=None` → D applies (falsifier: forwarding None as "wait forever" fails this). `(None, None)` → no timeout for that call.
+- [x] Every redirect hop uses the same effective timeout as the first request (default or override).
+- [x] Direct `Session.send(prepared)` with no timeout kwarg → D applies.
+- [x] No default configured (plain `HTTPAdapter()`, `requests.get`) → exactly as before: Timeout(connect=None, read=None).
+- [x] Invalid default (wrong-arity tuple, non-numeric) rejected at adapter construction with a clear error; existing per-call invalid-tuple error unchanged.
+- [x] Default scoped by mount prefix: an adapter mounted on `https://` does not affect `http://`.
+- [x] Pickle round-trip keeps the default (adapter and session); state from an adapter pickled without the field → no default.
+- [x] Diff shows no `Session.timeout`, no `__attrs__` entry on Session, no timeout merging in `Session.request/send`.
+- [x] Suite: only the 4 known TestTimeout connect failures (baseline 4 failed / 615 passed / 15 skipped / 1 xfailed).
+
+**Preserve:**
+- All behavior when no default is configured, bit-for-bit (incl. error message for bad per-call tuples).
+- `BaseAdapter.send` contract; custom adapters that ignore the feature.
+
+**Do not optimize for:**
+- A Session-level convenience API; global/module defaults; a new timeout value-object hierarchy.
+
+## Worker handoff (drafted — do not execute before the build command)
+
+ROLE: implementation Worker (executed inline as a separated phase — no subagent facility in this host).
+DESIGN GOAL: one owner in the adapter for timeout selection + resolution; the default validated once at the
+boundary (construction), resolved by the same path as a per-call value.
+BEHAVIOR: the exit criteria above. TESTING: test-first; each criterion its own test.
+PRESERVE / NON-GOALS: as above; match the grain of adapters.py (plain attributes, `__attrs__` pickling).
+RETURN: design reasoning, subtractive pass, result.
+
+## Open assumptions (unproven — carried, not filed)
+
+- none
+
+## Open Guide TODO
+
+- [x] Supersede-or-honor: honored (PO, 2026-09-23). Default lives in the transport adapter.
+- [x] Measure the build against every exit criterion myself (tests + diff read).
+- [x] File records: adapters.py companion (None semantics + why), sessions.py companion (where the need went).
+
+## Last evaluated result
+
+met — measured by the Guide: full suite 4 failed (the known env TestTimeout connect tests) / 644 passed
+(baseline 615 + 29 new) / 15 skipped / 1 xfailed; refactor step (extract `_resolve_timeout`) verified green on
+its own before the feature; `sessions.py` diff empty; mutation checks (drop `__attrs__` entry, drop class-level
+default) each caught by a pickling test. Worker phase ran inline (no subagent facility); panel-plan declined
+for the same reason.
