     r = requests.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)
 
+Default timeout for a Session
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+To avoid repeating ``timeout=`` on every call, give the session's
+:ref:`transport adapters <transport-adapters>` a default. Every request sent
+through them uses it unless the call passes its own ``timeout``::
+
+    from requests.adapters import HTTPAdapter
+
+    s = requests.Session()
+    adapter = HTTPAdapter(timeout=(3.05, 27))
+    s.mount('http://', adapter)
+    s.mount('https://', adapter)
+
+    s.get('https://github.com')              # uses (3.05, 27)
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=60)  # this call uses 60
+
+The default belongs to the adapter, so it applies only under the prefixes the
+adapter is mounted on, and to every redirect it follows. While an adapter has
+a default, ``timeout=None`` also means "use the default", so a ``None`` passed
+through by wrapper code cannot switch it off. To let one call wait without a
+limit, pass ``timeout=(None, None)``.
+
 .. note:: The connect timeout applies to each connection attempt to an IP address.
           If multiple addresses exist for a domain name, the underlying ``urllib3`` will
           try each address sequentially until one successfully connects.
